{"title":"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 32","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(guess_and_check)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (guess and check)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In this figure the center of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f9499af4d735d5e66f44bc4f185a0fedbcdbb51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB \\perp BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/7/c977d74a7e9f99d3a64318cc130708331f75bec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADOE$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is a straight line, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80d3368c5544e88d65c00bd70006b87f0f63bc39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = AD$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> has a length twice the radius. Then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/31001830291c125521d5551ec5ec3990ff4aa5c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)+fontsize(10)); real e=350,c=55; pair O=origin,E=dir(e),C=dir(c),B=dir(180+c),D=dir(180+e), rot=rotate(90,B)*O,A=extension(E,D,B,rot); path tangent=A--B; pair P=waypoint(tangent,abs(A-D)/abs(A-B)); draw(unitcircle^^C--B--A--E); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E^^P,linewidth(2)); label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,dir(290)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,dir(120)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,SE); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,SW);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"145\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1f1ef989b1a85ebafe55678c33b23ccc611b2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} AP^2 = PB \\times AB\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(B)}\\ AP \\times DO = PB \\times AD\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ AB^2 = AD \\times DE\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ AB \\times AD = OB \\times AO\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"218\" height=\"98\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" /> is the right answer.\n</p><p>Let the radius of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and let the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/849d923170c6cfab5b8b2d95ff5a7a1ede5b04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f9499af4d735d5e66f44bc4f185a0fedbcdbb51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB \\perp BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is a tangent to circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, by the tangent-secant theorem, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/4/ad4335d6a9a944727e26f5d2281e56d4c0fba0a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^2=AD\\times AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />, or, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b09bfd331b330940026bbb87dd78944f86ace6da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2r)^2=x(x+2r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"21\" />. Through some algebraic manipulation, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5eb51de0d9a7389609b60a0613b9f65e7ea21e41.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align}AD^2=x^2=2r(2r-x)\\end{align}\" width=\"330\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8785ca641359ef4ed47336514688721abe74fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD^2=AP^2=x^2$\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaaba474c38e0c7c5a708aae078f9ddc079f68b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB=AB-AP=2r-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"208\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/822e35cd4a9074a4e2620bbd7ff3eb756948f2db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=2r$\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> is identical to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbd61d8734064387c5c75015c3ff263b3a7f7d7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP^2=PB\\times AB$\" width=\"138\" height=\"15\" />, hence our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28guess_and_check.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(guess_and_check)\">Solution 2 (guess and check)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (guess and check)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of the circle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a4732815a51195ca49dd0b5e3466529ca1adf7d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 2r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />.  By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d7819bc5bb3f5b13cbce0745303b4ac3230f494b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO = \\sqrt{(2r)^2 + r^2} = r \\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"205\" height=\"32\" />.  That means, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e007de699acf024381204d253c37741570245b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = AP = r \\sqrt{5} - r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/b/f9b85b734c2343d76e2891ffcf083120cacf4407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB = 2r - r\\sqrt{5} + r = 3r - r\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"254\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Substitute values for each answer choice to determine which one is correct for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>For option A, substitution results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef7ae299a5f3e774e6af51718a14faa9acdea93a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(r \\sqrt{5} - r)^2 = (3r - r\\sqrt{5})2r\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b9b7e41f43196f349a86a1903f3267aac307f80.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5r^2 - 2r^2 \\sqrt{5} + r^2 = 6r^2 - 2r^2 \\sqrt{5}\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afde06c047018b7f7431544822e170d702f3d10e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6r^2 - 2r^2 \\sqrt{5} = 6r^2 - 2r^2 \\sqrt{5}\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>For option B, substitution results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a78d15ad3a21ce145ae9e486c4f38a44ff313104.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(r \\sqrt{5} - r)r = (3r - r\\sqrt{5})(r \\sqrt{5} - r)\\]\" width=\"273\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/803cf4c5607ec484de920064b585358c85446793.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2 \\sqrt{5} - r^2 = 4r^2 \\sqrt{5} - 8r^2\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>For option C, substitution results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/156080fe58839800a4e7624466d43e3f67717edf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2r)^2 = (r\\sqrt{5} - r)2r\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/b/cdb5f0a26b1f4d0267b4d5a5a4b6c32574dab67e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4r^2 = 2r^2 \\sqrt{5} - 2r^2\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>For option D, substitution results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/9297d09225fcba99abe9101368c43c3671f683e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(r \\sqrt{5} - r) \\cdot 2r = r \\cdot r\\sqrt{5}\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88e5ea240a56674bc3b70941e0b3dac7fbbfe93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2r^2 \\sqrt{5} - 2r^2 = r^2 \\sqrt{5}\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>From each option, only option A has both sides equaling each other, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME\" title=\"1960 AHSME\">1960 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1960 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1960\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 31\">Problem 31</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 33\">Problem 33</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\